# Optional TURN relay. Without it the game is STUN-only, which is what it
# shipped as: most pairs connect directly, and roughly 8-15% cannot connect
# at all. Setting these up is docs/turn.md.
#
# Copy to .env for local builds. In CI these come from repository secrets
# (TURN_URLS / TURN_USERNAME / TURN_CREDENTIAL) - see the deploy workflow.
#
# Everything with a VITE_ prefix is compiled into the bundle and is readable
# by anyone who opens devtools. That is unavoidable on a static host with no
# backend to mint short-lived credentials; the relay is protected by quotas
# and a restricted peer range instead. Nothing genuinely secret goes here.

# UDP first, TCP as a fallback for networks that block UDP outright.
VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:159.223.6.35:3478,turn:159.223.6.35:3478?transport=tcp,turns:turn.aytingchi.uz:443
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=monopoly
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=change-me
